+
+### Quantize pipeline colour outputs
+
+`fragment_color::quantize_fragment_color_outputs` can specialize an already
+translated fragment module for a caller-owned numeric attachment encoding.
+Use checked `AffineColorEncoding` values and one `FragmentColorEncoding` per
+selected location. The pass replaces direct float16/float32 RGBA outputs with
+Float32 outputs containing the decoded rounded integer values. It preserves
+unrelated interfaces and descriptor bindings; normal returns write the new
+outputs, while discarded invocations do not.
+
+This pass does not implement blending. Disable fixed-function blending at the
+selected locations and supply canonical clear/load contents. Quantization must
+follow the blend when blending is required. The caller must validate the returned
+module for its Vulkan environment, check Float32 attachment support, preserve
+attachment write masks, and handle MSAA resolve quantization separately.
+Unsupported output types, pointer escapes, grouped/component decorations, or
+multiple entry points return `ColorQuantizationRefusal`. No device format names
+or memory-plane policy enter this API.
 
